From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:13:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Default resized images to quality 80 and pre-render the
 shapes clients ask for

A client that sends maxWidth/maxHeight but no quality got quality 100: a
300 px poster was ~113 KB against ~28 KB at 80 with no visible difference
on a TV. Requests without any resize keep 100, so the original file is
still served untouched.

The first request for each size costs a 130-280 ms resize on a slow CPU.
The image cache key holds the exact maxWidth and output format, so a fixed
list of sizes can't be guessed: ImageShapeTracker counts the resize shapes
actually served (persisted to data/image-shapes.json, capped at 256), and
the daily "Pre-render images" task renders the top shapes for items added
in the last 7 days, then halves the counts so old layouts fade out.
